nd lo and behold a page with directions  with routes prices six grand to come to  the united states  9 300 to get to san antonio it takes  a simple search of get to the front  and that is all it takes to find out  exactly who to pay  how to get here and how you're going to  get smuggled across and they even talk  about in these ads  how you can take a six-year-old or under  or if you're a single adult what they're  going to do to help get you across  it's absolutely nuts it is nuts be and  they know that if you've got a kid  they're going to let the kid in and they  might let you in as well  but here's the thing and you've written  a letter to  facebook and you've written a letter to  mark zuckerberg to say hey  look what you're doing but think about  it  this means that facebook is making  money from cartels and from human  smugglers  how can they do that it's absolutely i  mean  27 billion dollars is what facebook made  in the first quarter of this year  now i'm not saying that that's all  cartel money right but they are  advertising on social media but then if  you look in my own home district  i have a little mom and pop shop owned  by the lrads they sell homemade jellies  and they were banned from selling  advertisements on facebook  because they had been flagged for  conservative content  i have a single mom in ocala who owns a  video production company and she's been  banned from selling ads on facebook  because she posted a picture of herself  in a maga hat this  is unconscionable so my my question to  mark zuckerberg and the folks at  facebook  instead of targeting conservatives maybe  we should focus on the cartels instead  right yeah no kidding well let's see  what they do i know that after you wrote  your letter it was a big  story and yet you just did a search 37  minutes ago  and the ads are still there that it's  just yeah  congresswoman before you go we were  talking a moment ago about earmarks uh  so are you one of the republican  congress people who have signed up for  more government cash for your district  no i can say that i am proud to have  voted against earmarks and stood firm  against them  washington's got a spending problem uh  not a saving  problem so i think i can better serve my  constituents by working to recover money  that's already owed to them through  federal agencies rather than spending  more of their hard-earned tax dollars  there you go  all right congresswoman kat kamek  joining us from gainesville  thank you very much for joining us live  there was some concern whether or not i  would pronounce her last name correctly  and i think i did at the end  all right thank you congresswoman
 

